    <fr:title text="Forest capture server">Forest capture server</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p><html:code>~/nix-config/hosts/macproseph/capture-server.py</html:code>, reachable at <html:code>http://macproseph:8889/capture</html:code> over Tailscale.</html:p>
    <html:ul><html:li>Four payload shapes: JSON prose, JSON verbatim, JSON webclip, multipart+form, raw-body file</html:li>
  <html:li>Every capture gets an ISO-8601 UTC <html:code><![CDATA[\date]]></html:code> — required for the dashboard's "most recent" pane to surface it</html:li>
  <html:li>PDFs land as <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{pdf}{\route-asset{...}}]]></html:code> (theme renders a viewer); images embed via inline <html:code><![CDATA[\<html:img>]]></html:code>; other files link through <html:code><![CDATA[\a]]></html:code></html:li>
  <html:li><html:code>kick_sync</html:code> runs in a worker thread that waits for idle then blocking-starts <html:code>forest-pull.service</html:code>, then re-runs if more captures arrived during the cycle — without this, a capture landing mid-build is read after the build's input pass and never makes it to <html:code>output/</html:code></html:li></html:ul>
  </fr:mainmatter>
