                <fr:title text="Home server (macproseph)">Home server (macproseph)</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>Serve the forest on the Tailscale network so iPad/phone can browse it.</html:p>
                <html:ul><html:li>Clone the forest repo to <html:code>/home/steven/forest</html:code></html:li>
  <html:li>Run <html:code>forester build forest.toml</html:code> on a 15-minute systemd timer, producing <html:code>output/</html:code></html:li>
  <html:li>Serve <html:code>output/</html:code> statically via caddy on port 8888 (Tailscale-only)</html:li>
  <html:li><html:code>forest-pull.service</html:code> commits local captures, rebases against origin, pushes, then chains into <html:code>forest-build.service</html:code></html:li></html:ul>
                <html:p>We originally planned <html:code>forester serve</html:code> (HTMX mode), but hit URL routing bugs — the slug link generator builds <html:code>/HOST/X/</html:code> paths that don't match the server's <html:code>/trees/X</html:code> router. Static build sidesteps this; the XSLT link routing emits relative hrefs which work from any origin.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
