            <fr:title text="Debug: Dashboard Not Updating After Sync on macproseph">Debug: Dashboard Not Updating After Sync on macproseph</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>TODO</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="status">done</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="priority">high</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="completed">2026-04-17</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="apple-id">x-apple-reminder://BF64B5FB-3150-4A97-BACF-BA8D1ABAE4FF</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="forester-addr">sss-009F</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>New trees are successfully synced to macproseph (pulled from origin), but the dashboard's Datalog queries are not reflecting them — the dashboard appears stale even though the tree files are present on disk.</html:p>
            <html:p>Server configuration lives in <html:code>~/nix-config/hosts/macproseph/</html:code>. The sync pipeline is documented in <fr:link href="/sss-0088/" title="Forest Sync and Capture Architecture" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-0088/" display-uri="sss-0088" type="local">Forest Sync and Capture Architecture</fr:link>; the capture server's <html:code>kick_sync</html:code> flow (which chains <html:code>forest-pull.service</html:code> → <html:code>forest-build.service</html:code>) is described in <fr:link href="/sss-008M/" title="Forest capture server" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-008M/" display-uri="sss-008M" type="local">Forest capture server</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>Possible causes to investigate:</html:p>
            <html:ul><html:li><html:code>forest-build.service</html:code> not triggering after a pull-only sync (i.e. when macproseph pulls from origin but no capture happened, so <html:code>kick_sync</html:code> never fires)</html:li>
  <html:li><html:code>forester build</html:code> running before the pull completes, so new trees aren't on disk yet when the build reads inputs</html:li>
  <html:li>Caddy serving stale output from a previous build — check whether caddy is configured with <html:code>file_server</html:code> pointing at the live <html:code>output/</html:code> directory or a cached copy</html:li>
  <html:li>Datalog query cache inside forester not invalidated across builds (less likely; forester rebuilds from scratch)</html:li>
  <html:li>The systemd timer for <html:code>forest-pull.service</html:code> not actually firing — verify with <html:code>systemctl status forest-pull.timer</html:code> and <html:code>journalctl -u forest-pull.service</html:code></html:li></html:ul>
            <html:p>Debugging checklist:</html:p>
            <html:ul><html:li>SSH into macproseph; confirm new tree files are present under <html:code>/home/steven/forest/trees/</html:code></html:li>
  <html:li>Check <html:code>journalctl -u forest-build.service</html:code> to see whether a build ran after the most recent pull and what its exit status was</html:li>
  <html:li>Inspect the <html:code>output/</html:code> directory mtime — is it newer than the pulled tree files?</html:li>
  <html:li>Check <html:code>~/nix-config/hosts/macproseph/</html:code> for the systemd unit definitions and confirm the dependency chain between pull and build services</html:li>
  <html:li>Re-run <html:code>forester build --dev forest.toml</html:code> manually on macproseph and verify the dashboard reflects the new trees</html:li></html:ul>
            <html:p><html:strong>Resolution.</html:strong> Root cause: <html:code>forest.toml</html:code> has <html:code>exclude_tags = ["private", "draft"]</html:code> for the public website build, but macproseph was using the same config. The dashboard tree carries <html:code><![CDATA[\tag{private}]]></html:code>, so forester skipped regenerating its output page on every build — leaving a stale snapshot from April 15. Fix: added <html:code>macproseph.toml</html:code> (no <html:code>exclude_tags</html:code>) and updated <html:code>forest.nix</html:code> to use it. Dashboard now rebuilds correctly every 15 minutes.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
